both of them so well, and it's a joy to have you as a teacher.

1341
01:40:38,201 --> 01:40:41,264
I want to put emphasis on the word joy.

1342
01:40:41,283 --> 01:40:45,970
Grateful in the midst of all the confusion and despair.

1343
01:40:46,069 --> 01:40:48,431
So thanks very much.

1344
01:40:48,773 --> 01:40:52,577
Thank you.

1345
01:40:52,596 --> 01:40:57,922
And Bante, I thought I'd paralleled you a little bit.

1346
01:40:58,527 --> 01:41:05,917
in going to Trostle Hall as my first point of call for a Buddhist teaching.

1347
01:41:06,719 --> 01:41:08,882
I think I was possibly a few years behind you.

1348
01:41:10,043 --> 01:41:19,158
But I was struggling with their approach, which I found rather rigid and overly dogmatic and controlling.

1349
01:41:19,177 --> 01:41:26,509
So it was a great relief for me when I did a retreat with you and Ruat Adama in 87 in Birmingham.

1350
01:41:26,759 --> 01:41:42,819
It was quite a turning point for me, and it was a big turning point for our group when you came to Dublin the following year and moved in a more caravan way than a Zen way.

1351
01:41:43,381 --> 01:41:46,845
So thank you for your teaching over the years.

1352
01:41:49,948 --> 01:41:52,091
And I want to say that

1353
01:41:52,493 --> 01:41:58,578
Hearing the story about you rubbing cigarettes was so relieving.

1354
01:41:58,719 --> 01:42:02,743
On the first weekend we didn't know the room.

1355
01:42:03,243 --> 01:42:04,725
We didn't know we couldn't eat.

1356
01:42:05,525 --> 01:42:07,488
So we rubbed bananas in the kitchen.

1357
01:42:07,528 --> 01:42:11,131
I never told you that.

1358
01:42:11,152 --> 01:42:12,233
I'm getting it off my chest.

1359
01:42:13,213 --> 01:42:21,301
Absolutely.

1360
01:42:21,957 --> 01:42:41,890
so we just uh birthday again and i think it's gone and um uh i just want to wish you all wish you happy birthday from all of us and look forward to uh teachings in the future thank you thank you take care thank you

1361
01:42:45,987 --> 01:42:48,189
Where was I before that interruption?

1362
01:42:51,811 --> 01:42:52,193
Ah, he's gone.

1363
01:42:57,117 --> 01:43:02,101
You were talking about the woman who had gone to a monastery where she was the only woman.

1364
01:43:02,761 --> 01:43:03,842
Oh, yeah, that's Roshi Kennet.

1365
01:43:04,162 --> 01:43:05,725
Yeah, but I don't know what in context.

1366
01:43:06,185 --> 01:43:07,546
It's part of being 70.

1367
01:43:08,847 --> 01:43:09,528
I can't remember a thing.

1368
01:43:09,608 --> 01:43:10,009
It's great.

1369
01:43:11,750 --> 01:43:12,690
Every moment is new.

1370
01:43:15,193 --> 01:43:15,993
Who are you again?

1371
01:43:21,256 --> 01:43:21,979
the next 10 years?

1372
01:43:22,582 --> 01:43:22,844
Sorry?

1373
01:43:23,246 --> 01:43:25,033
What are your hopes for the next 10 years?

1374
01:43:25,797 --> 01:43:27,064
That I continue to live.

1375
01:43:29,018 --> 01:43:30,539
I think I need a bit more time to...

1376
01:43:32,563 --> 01:43:35,927
I mean, what I would like is a halo of teachers.

1377
01:43:36,127 --> 01:43:36,569
Do you like that?

1378
01:43:37,229 --> 01:43:40,413
A halo of teachers to be established here.

1379
01:43:41,314 --> 01:43:43,118
Seven or eight of them.

1380
01:43:43,158 --> 01:43:46,322
So that the place just has that background of good teachers, you see.

1381
01:43:46,363 --> 01:43:47,604
At the moment we have three.

1382
01:43:48,045 --> 01:43:50,668
So there's Carl, Aya and Hus.

1383
01:43:50,948 --> 01:43:52,030
Put your hand up, Hus, please.

1384
01:43:52,091 --> 01:43:53,672
There we are, you see.

1385
01:43:54,274 --> 01:43:57,337
So it'd be nice to have that, you see.

1386
01:43:57,318 --> 01:44:14,854
and uh hopefully to find a way to run this place which uh doesn't depend on me that's that's my target for the next five years and then i'll disappear yeah that's that would be my hope anyway

1387
01:44:21,735 --> 01:44:27,764
No, I don't think, I'll only disappear when it's time to go.

1388
01:44:31,328 --> 01:44:46,426
I'm wondering about the, you talked before about Gaia House and the dilemma of becoming a layperson and disrobing and it's quite a new, well I suppose we think of

1389
01:44:46,659 --> 01:44:50,404
monks within a group and you've chosen to be on your own.

1390
01:44:50,444 --> 01:44:59,114
I just wonder about your commitment to being in robes and to sticking with the monastic order despite, but not being with other people.

1391
01:44:59,135 --> 01:45:00,617
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1392
01:45:00,997 --> 01:45:01,618
No, that's true.

1393
01:45:01,658 --> 01:45:02,838
Lone monks are known.

1394
01:45:02,878 --> 01:45:07,864
You will get monks who are quite happy to be on their own.

1395
01:45:07,925 --> 01:45:11,149
It's not a choice, it's just the way I've ended up.

1396
01:45:11,128 --> 01:45:18,421
There are no Western monks that I was involved with in Sri Lanka who could have come over with me.

1397
01:45:18,802 --> 01:45:19,604
There just weren't any.

1398
01:45:20,045 --> 01:45:20,645
That's the end of it.

1399
01:45:20,787 --> 01:45:22,930
So I was basically on my own from the beginning, you see.

1400
01:45:26,015 --> 01:45:32,427
It would have been nice to have had a partner or somebody to run the place, somebody whom you're compatible with.

1401
01:45:33,269 --> 01:45:36,774
You have to remember that just because you're a monk doesn't mean you like the person.

1402
01:45:39,198 --> 01:45:40,301
It's a varied community.

1403
01:45:42,203 --> 01:45:48,274
But there have been many times throughout the 30 years, this is my 30th year, where I've wanted to leave.

1404
01:45:49,015 --> 01:45:53,804
There was one point where I was going to bed saying, right, tomorrow that's it, we'll get out, we'll do something useful.

1405
01:45:54,085 --> 01:45:56,588
And I wake up in the morning and I'd say, well, God, I'll give you just one more day.

1406
01:45:57,210 --> 01:45:58,972
And in the end, I just had to laugh.

1407
01:45:58,953 --> 01:46:04,885
Now, every time I came to this point of wanting to leave, I couldn't think of anything at all in society that attracted me.

1408
01:46:05,265 --> 01:46:06,146
I went through the whole job.

1409
01:46:06,427 --> 01:46:11,677
And I usually ended up with a fantasy of stacking shelves and going back to the garret and doing my meditation.

1410
01:46:12,139 --> 01:46:13,801
So I said, well, I can do that without stacking shelves.

1411
01:46:17,588 --> 01:46:18,530
So I never left.

1412
01:46:19,033 --> 01:46:23,119
Every time that, you know, there were times when I was very close.

1413
01:46:23,860 --> 01:46:27,364
One of them was at the end of that escapade up in North London.

1414
01:46:27,786 --> 01:46:31,110
I mean, that was an obvious time where, you know, I didn't know where to go.

1415
01:46:31,610 --> 01:46:32,192
It was nowhere.

1416
01:46:32,212 --> 01:46:37,939
But I just, there was nothing I, I just ended up faffing about.

1417
01:46:39,641 --> 01:46:40,342
And what about the robes?

1418
01:46:40,363 --> 01:46:44,469
What about the actual... Robes?

1419
01:46:44,970 --> 01:46:46,712
Well, I'm stuck with the colour.

1420
01:46:47,840 --> 01:46:53,006
I mean, I'd love to wear blue.

1421
01:46:53,027 --> 01:46:53,887
You know, pink.

1422
01:46:54,148 --> 01:46:54,849
I'd love to wear pink.

1423
01:46:55,690 --> 01:46:56,511
See, I look pink.

1424
01:46:57,233 --> 01:46:57,573
Pink-like.

1425
01:46:57,592 --> 01:47:00,115
What do you mean by the robes?

1426
01:47:00,317 --> 01:47:05,182
Well, I suppose, why not just become a layperson?

1427
01:47:05,283 --> 01:47:06,024
Oh, I see.

1428
01:47:06,043 --> 01:47:06,204
Ah.

1429
01:47:07,305 --> 01:47:08,127
Oh, very good.

1430
01:47:09,088 --> 01:47:12,132
Hello.

1431
01:47:12,313 --> 01:47:15,216
Hello, greetings from... Hooray!

1432
01:47:15,237 --> 01:47:15,417
Hooray!

1433
01:47:18,163 --> 01:47:19,145
Very good.

1434
01:47:19,324 --> 01:47:20,407
How are you?

1435
01:47:20,667 --> 01:47:23,329
We have one teenager here in pyjamas, Bante.

1436
01:47:23,350 --> 01:47:27,695
Is that okay if she appears?

1437
01:47:27,716 --> 01:47:28,176
Alicia.

1438
01:47:28,195 --> 01:47:29,597
She's wearing pyjamas.

1439
01:47:31,319 --> 01:47:32,421
Yes, that's all right.

1440
01:47:32,601 --> 01:47:35,465
Thank you for giving me birthday greetings.

1441
01:47:35,546 --> 01:47:36,646
Oh, very good.

1442
01:47:38,789 --> 01:47:43,956
We wanted to show you the birthday cake that we'll be celebrating your birthday with.

1443
01:47:44,155 --> 01:47:44,976
Oh, fancy.

1444
01:47:46,078 --> 01:47:47,260
So we're just...

1445
01:47:47,560 --> 01:47:56,354
bring it a little bit closer.

1446
01:48:07,135 --> 01:48:09,698
You'll be eating your words very soon, Banting.

1447
01:48:16,847 --> 01:48:22,916
The cards that we sent based on some of the memories that we have from visiting.

1448
01:48:22,935 --> 01:48:28,882
I just wanted to share one little story that we still find amusing.

1449
01:48:28,984 --> 01:48:33,970
And it was the time that we climbed up Mount Banting.

1450
01:48:36,159 --> 01:48:49,917
And for those of you who don't know where it is, it's a mountain of spiritual significance here in West Kerry, named after St. Brandon the Navigator, who went to the shores to America.

1451
01:48:50,877 --> 01:49:02,271
So a few years ago, we hiked up with Bunty, right at the top where there's a beautiful Catholic cross and an inscription and a little cairn of stones.

1452
01:49:02,351 --> 01:49:03,753
So Bunty decided,

1453
01:49:04,087 --> 01:49:12,221
at the top of the mountain on a clear blue sky day, very calm, that he would chant.

1454
01:49:13,423 --> 01:49:21,979
So he sat in the little cairn and he began his chant, his Pally chant, which we joined in, and then suddenly this wind whipped up

1455
01:49:23,207 --> 01:49:25,793
started blowing around us at the top of the mountain.

1456
01:49:25,833 --> 01:49:36,176
And Bhante put up his hands and he said, the wrath of St. Brendan is upon you.

1457
01:49:36,195 --> 01:49:39,864
That's one of the memories we have from one of your visits here to us, Bhante.

1458
01:49:42,930 --> 01:49:43,292
Thank you.

1459
01:49:43,627 --> 01:50:06,056
anything else anything uh bandy uh john here just to uh wish you a happy birthday thank you that's your first 10-day retreat uh you uh performed in the pub view hostel for 20 years ago so uh you've gone from strength to strength and uh we thank you for your inspiration

1460
01:50:07,640 --> 01:50:08,561
Thank you very much.

1461
01:50:09,082 --> 01:50:09,805
Thank you very much.

1462
01:50:10,345 --> 01:50:10,947
Keep the cake.

1463
01:50:12,751 --> 01:50:15,817
I'm coming.

1464
01:50:15,837 --> 01:50:19,585
If we could keep you in peace, we would, but we'll send you photos of it.

1465
01:50:20,105 --> 01:50:24,034
We're just going to light the candles now and sing you out from West Kerry.

1466
01:50:24,676 --> 01:50:26,560
Thank you very much.

1467
01:50:27,180 --> 01:50:56,158
you know come on we're going to sing it in irish fenty happy birthday to you in irish you've had it in pali and you're getting the gaelic version now

1468
01:50:56,391 --> 01:51:11,818
Thank you very much.

1469
01:51:11,837 --> 01:51:13,319
I'll eat the head.

1470
01:51:24,167 --> 01:51:27,051
What's your funniest teaching experience?

1471
01:51:27,072 --> 01:51:28,413
Funniest teaching experience?

1472
01:51:29,274 --> 01:51:29,836
Can't think of any.

1473
01:51:30,036 --> 01:51:32,219
What do you mean by that?

1474
01:51:32,238 --> 01:51:34,823
Actually, you've got a question to answer as well.

1475
01:51:36,225 --> 01:51:38,528
You answer her question.

1476
01:51:38,707 --> 01:51:39,609
That was about the robes.

1477
01:51:40,270 --> 01:51:40,872
See, I remembered.

1478
01:51:42,193 --> 01:51:43,375
The robes.

1479
01:51:43,743 --> 01:51:45,225
Why don't I?

1480
01:51:45,345 --> 01:51:45,845
Oh, I see.

1481
01:51:46,367 --> 01:51:52,796
Well, the robes are a guardian, really, because you have to behave in a certain way when you walk around in robes.

1482
01:51:53,978 --> 01:51:55,860
But it's just, you just get used to it.

1483
01:51:55,881 --> 01:51:57,684
I haven't even thought about that, really.

1484
01:51:57,724 --> 01:52:07,859
The question was about, you know, other than that, have you thought about being a Dharma teacher?

1485
01:52:08,298 --> 01:52:09,942
Oh, yeah.

1486
01:52:10,162 --> 01:52:13,546
Yeah, but it doesn't attract me because...

1487
01:52:14,506 --> 01:52:20,672
Dharma teachers, they get support, but remember they've got massive overheads.

1488
01:52:21,474 --> 01:52:25,618
Sometimes they have children, they have cars to run, all that sort of stuff.

1489
01:52:27,440 --> 01:52:31,086
Being a monk really releases me from all that sort of baggage.

1490
01:52:31,626 --> 01:52:36,311
You shouldn't call it baggage really, you should call it delight.

1491
01:52:38,079 --> 01:52:40,403
Releases me from the delight of all my life.

1492
01:52:42,185 --> 01:52:48,796
So that my, you know, once I've got my laptop and stuff like that, that's it.

1493
01:52:50,297 --> 01:52:56,367
If I left, it would, I don't know, it just doesn't attract me.

1494
01:52:57,047 --> 01:52:58,411
I mean, I'm conditioned now.

1495
01:52:59,112 --> 01:53:01,716
It takes such a long time to recondition yourself, you know.

1496
01:53:01,956 --> 01:53:04,720
I just feel comfortable in the rows.

1497
01:53:05,320 --> 01:53:06,061
It's as simple as that.

1498
01:53:07,443 --> 01:53:10,225
And I haven't got long to go anyway.

1499
01:53:10,244 --> 01:53:14,609
Ah!

1500
01:53:14,649 --> 01:53:15,170
Hello, Mike.

1501
01:53:16,251 --> 01:53:17,511
Our building consultant.

1502
01:53:18,752 --> 01:53:20,613
Upon whom we are dependent.

1503
01:53:23,997 --> 01:53:24,136
Hi.

1504
01:53:25,639 --> 01:53:26,118
Hi, Vandy.

1505
01:53:26,319 --> 01:53:26,680
Hi.

1506
01:53:27,020 --> 01:53:27,980
Well, happy birthday.

1507
01:53:28,041 --> 01:53:28,480
Thank you.

1508
01:53:29,442 --> 01:53:30,643
I'm getting distracted here.

1509
01:53:30,662 --> 01:53:34,305
I've got two things going on at once.

1510
01:53:34,787 --> 01:53:36,488
There seems to be a delay on the...

1511
01:53:37,430 --> 01:53:38,832
Can you hear me?

1512
01:53:38,931 --> 01:53:40,073
Yes, yes.

1513
01:53:41,916 --> 01:53:43,938
Well, happy birthday.

1514
01:53:44,057 --> 01:53:45,060
Thank you.

1515
01:53:45,239 --> 01:53:56,554
And thank you so much for all the teachings you gave me over the years that we've been building together.

1516
01:53:56,914 --> 01:54:06,407
There was one incident that actually typifies you, which you probably actually forgot, but we were away in Suffolk

1517
01:54:07,045 --> 01:54:08,346
And we went to a church.

1518
01:54:09,529 --> 01:54:13,676
And whilst we were wandering around, the verger came out and gave us a guided tour.

1519
01:54:14,738 --> 01:54:31,887
And there was a chap came into the church who was distressed, didn't have any money to get home, was obviously in an incredibly bad way.

1520
01:54:32,712 --> 01:54:39,658
before the verger could actually say anything, you'd put your hand in your pocket and gave the guy five quid.

1521
01:54:39,679 --> 01:54:46,805
And the verger was so blown away, he couldn't believe your generosity and your instant kindness.

1522
01:54:47,987 --> 01:54:52,912
And that's a memory that sticks with me when I think of most of the song.

1523
01:54:52,931 --> 01:54:53,912
Thank you very much, mate.

1524
01:54:54,033 --> 01:54:57,657
It was a very...

1525
01:54:59,779 --> 01:55:06,127
generous moment, and it just typified your embodying loving-kindness.

1526
01:55:06,146 --> 01:55:08,791
It was really a nice moment.

1527
01:55:08,810 --> 01:55:10,712
Yeah, that was a good moment I had.

1528
01:55:16,579 --> 01:55:17,761
Well, we all love them sometimes.

1529
01:55:18,442 --> 01:55:19,823
Exactly that.

1530
01:55:23,427 --> 01:55:23,847
Take care.

1531
01:55:24,349 --> 01:55:27,912
Well, I hope there's another 70 years worth of

1532
01:55:28,753 --> 01:55:33,881
That is influence, if not presence, in South Manion.

1533
01:55:34,103 --> 01:55:36,145
Certainly the building will last another 70 years.

1534
01:55:36,206 --> 01:55:36,386
Yes.

1535
01:55:48,905 --> 01:55:49,828
I'll see you Thursday.

1536
01:55:52,270 --> 01:55:56,398
Yes.

1537
01:55:57,204 --> 01:55:59,787
It's coming up to check it out.

1538
01:56:08,880 --> 01:56:10,481
A funny teaching moment, I can't think.

1539
01:56:15,027 --> 01:56:15,667
Pam?

1540
01:56:15,688 --> 01:56:17,489
This is sort of related to that.

1541
01:56:17,510 --> 01:56:21,255
I've known you for a really long time.

1542
01:56:23,193 --> 01:56:24,154
Yes.

1543
01:56:24,175 --> 01:56:31,605
And you always were really, really, really funny and I think you're still really funny and so do lots of people.

1544
01:56:31,645 --> 01:56:33,828
Really appreciate your sense of humour.

1545
01:56:34,449 --> 01:56:39,698
How important do you think a sense of humour is in the spiritual life?

1546
01:56:40,219 --> 01:56:43,404
Not just yours, but everybody's spiritual life.

1547
01:56:43,444 --> 01:56:46,668
Do you think that the sense of humour has a place?

1548
01:56:47,779 --> 01:56:52,546
Well, definitely, it's catching the irony, isn't it?

1549
01:56:52,606 --> 01:56:57,233
It's catching the paradox, seeing the paradox.

1550
01:56:57,273 --> 01:57:06,204
Remember, in Zen Buddhism, once you break through the delusion, there's this great guffaw, this great laugh that it's all been this stupid mistake.

1551
01:57:06,765 --> 01:57:08,047
Now you've messed up.

1552
01:57:09,710 --> 01:57:10,690
Oh, hello.

1553
01:57:11,813 --> 01:57:12,613
Ricardo, come in.

1554
01:57:14,036 --> 01:57:15,778
Is that over now, is it?

1555
01:57:16,534 --> 01:57:17,896
Ah, that's it.

1556
01:57:18,518 --> 01:57:19,418
Fantastic.

1557
01:57:19,439 --> 01:57:21,922
Thank you very much.

1558
01:57:29,875 --> 01:57:31,337
So, yes, how are we doing for time?

1559
01:57:32,057 --> 01:57:32,639
Tea time, is it?

1560
01:57:33,180 --> 01:57:37,627
No, there's stuff to do, yeah.

1561
01:57:38,828 --> 01:57:38,929
Oh.

1562
01:57:39,810 --> 01:57:40,971
So, yes, humour.

1563
01:57:41,693 --> 01:57:41,832
Humour.

1564
01:57:44,345 --> 01:57:51,713
I'd like to take this opportunity to present you with a cheque, quite a large cheque.

1565
01:57:53,817 --> 01:57:57,180
This is donations, as you know, from all of the Sangha.

1566
01:57:58,983 --> 01:58:05,390
A very generous offer has been made to round up what was donated to give us this figure.

1567
01:58:06,130 --> 01:58:08,893
of 7,070 pounds and 70 pence.

1568
01:58:09,193 --> 01:58:10,534
My goodness, look at that.

1569
01:58:10,555 --> 01:58:11,836
70, 70, 70.

1570
01:58:12,176 --> 01:58:13,117
That's not bad, is it?

1571
01:58:13,136 --> 01:58:14,057
70, 70, 70.

1572
01:58:14,078 --> 01:58:25,970
Yeah, I'm particularly relieved because it means I can get a return ticket.

1573
01:58:29,335 --> 01:58:30,636
That's wonderful, thank you.

1574
01:58:34,868 --> 01:58:37,390
No, no, it's not.

1575
01:58:37,430 --> 01:58:38,712
No, it's not.

1576
01:58:38,792 --> 01:58:41,655
No, no, I'm joking.

1577
